    "Labels were read through a text-extraction fetch of the PCNE PDF (direct download from pcne.org was refused by this session's network proxy). The extraction gave the code and label lines; a pharmacist should check every label against the PDF before signing.",
    "Only the short labels are captured. PCNE's explanatory notes per code (for example what counts as 'Intervention discussed' versus 'proposed') are thin in V9.1 itself; the separate help text and the extended scoring form (418_DRP-form_ext_V9-1.pdf) were not opened.",
    "Each Problem is also marked Potential or Manifest (tick boxes on the form). This is a property of the problem record, not a code, so it is not in the code list; MedSync needs a separate field for it.",
    "Ellipses in I3.1 to I3.4 ('Drug changed to ...') stand for free text in the original; they are written here as three full stops.",
    "No commercial-use permission has been requested or granted. The licence position must be settled by the MedSync owner with the PCNE Board (drp@pcne.org) before any of this is shown to users.",
    "No newer version (V10) was found on pcne.org on the access date; the site says major changes must wait for a totally new version, with no timeline.",
    "None of these codes is signed. Every mapping from MedSync query types to PCNE in MEDREC-PCNE.md is a candidate draft for the pharmacist reviewer and the Clinical Safety Officer."
